cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  libmatch: code and result tables for "Library size and sequence
  relatedness confound comparisons between synthetic benchmarks and
  experimental antibody data"
message: >-
  If you use this software or the result tables, please cite both the software
  and the article it accompanies.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dohun
    family-names: Kim
    email: dohun@etri.re.kr
    affiliation: >-
      Autonomous Intelligence DX Research Section, Electronics and
      Telecommunications Research Institute
  - given-names: Minho
    family-names: Bae
    affiliation: >-
      Autonomous Intelligence DX Research Section, Electronics and
      Telecommunications Research Institute
abstract: >-
  libmatch measures five properties of a sequence-label dataset - size,
  structure, alignability, label origin and measurement noise - and reports
  which of them differ between two datasets being compared. The repository also
  holds the scripts, result tables and matched libraries behind the article,
  with a generated reproduction map from every reported number to the script
  that produced it.
keywords:
  - antibody
  - machine learning
  - benchmark
  - dataset comparability
  - reproducibility
  - protein engineering
license: MIT
version: 1.0.4
repository-code: https://github.com/kdh6126/libmatch
